# WBC Transfer Evaluation

**Adaptation-free external evaluation of retinal- and ImageNet-pretrained white blood cell classifiers**

This repository supports the revised study:

> *Evaluating Cross-Domain Transfer and Adaptation-Free External Generalization of Retinal- and ImageNet-Pretrained Models for White Blood Cell Classification* (Applied Sciences, manuscript `applsci-4726214`).

The study compares **ResNet-50**, **ConvNeXt-Tiny**, and **RETFound** on WBCBench 2026 (13 classes, seeds **42, 1, 7**) and external PBC and Raabin-WBC datasets. External evaluations use **frozen WBCBench-selected checkpoints**: no external-data fine-tuning, recalibration, or checkpoint selection.

**Version note:** This documentation is prepared for a **proposed v1.1 release** containing the corrected external RETFound evaluation, audited external results, BNE+SNE sensitivity, the Raabin-WBC TestB supplementary analysis, and per-class results for Reviewer 1.11. The repository's publicly accessible files and release assets have **not** been independently verified. Do **not** claim that the v1.1 files are public until they have been committed/tagged and the release has been published.

- Repository: https://github.com/sara-altun/WBC-Transfer-Evaluation
- Historical release: https://github.com/sara-altun/WBC-Transfer-Evaluation/releases/tag/v1.0
- Proposed revised release (after publication): https://github.com/sara-altun/WBC-Transfer-Evaluation/releases/tag/v1.1

## 1. Datasets and access

Download the datasets from their respective publishers; **raw images are not included** in this repository.

| Dataset | Original source | Use in the manuscript |
|---|---|---|
| **WBCBench 2026** | [Xin-Tian/wbcbench2026, Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Xin-Tian/wbcbench2026) | `phase2_train`, `phase2_eval`, and locked `phase2_test`; 13-class primary task, plus matched 5-class sensitivity |
| **PBC** | [Acevedo et al., Mendeley Data](https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/snkd93bnjr/1) | External five-class evaluation (10,298 readable images in the selected folders) |
| **Raabin-WBC** | [Official Raabin-WBC site](https://raabindata.com/free-data/) | `Train` (10,175) + `TestA` (4,339), five-class external evaluation; `TestB` evaluated separately |

The local WBCBench test set contains **32,934 image entries**, including pristine/degraded counterpart images. Its matched five-class subset includes **29,610 entries**. WBCBench split/group identifiers must not automatically be interpreted as proof of person-level independence. The specific historical WBCBench download revision should be archived or recorded separately, because label revisions can affect comparability.

The PBC candidate set included one unreadable image; the audited evaluation included 10,298 readable images, not 10,299 candidates. The separate Raabin-WBC **TestB** subset has **2,119 readable images (LY = 148, N = 1,971)**, with no BA, EO, or MO labels in the evaluated two-class subset. **TestB is not part of the five-class Train+TestA Macro-F1 result.** Its analysis tests a different, narrower task under distinct acquisition conditions.

Dataset citations and use restrictions remain those of the original publishers. The repository's code licence does not grant permission to redistribute third-party images or model weights.

## 2. Study protocol and class mapping

- **Models:** ImageNet-pretrained ResNet-50 and ConvNeXt-Tiny; retinal-CFP-pretrained RETFound, fully fine-tuned on WBCBench. These are comparisons of **model configurations**, not a causal isolation of pretraining source.
- **Seeds:** 42, 1, 7; checkpoint choice based on WBCBench validation Macro-F1 only.
- **Primary external task:** BA (basophil), EO (eosinophil), LY (lymphocyte), MO (monocyte), N (neutrophil). The five-class decision uses the corresponding BA, EO, LY, MO, SNE output scores of the 13-class models.
- **BNE+SNE sensitivity:** For the N decision score, combine the **band neutrophil (BNE)** and **segmented neutrophil (SNE)** probabilities; retain the other four scores.
- **RETFound correction:** Historical external predictions produced with a mismatched pooling configuration are **superseded**. Re-evaluation uses the trained RETFound `global_pool=True` architecture and matching final fine-tuned checkpoint parameters. The weights were not retrained for this correction.
- **Uncertainty:** External pairwise 95% intervals use 1,500 class-stratified, paired **image-level** bootstrap resamples, with the three-seed average difference as the statistic. They are **not** film- or patient-cluster intervals.
- **TestB interpretation:** Five-way LY/N recall is derived from the original five-output rule; *conditional two-class Macro-F1* is calculated only when the decision is restricted to LY and N. These are **different estimands**. Neither is directly comparable with the five-class Train+TestA Macro-F1.

## 3. Suggested local folder layout

These paths describe the **input/output layout expected by the notebooks**, not a claim that all folders are present in the public repository.

```text
WBC-Transfer-Evaluation/                       # local project root (formerly sci5-wbc)
├── README.md
├── LICENSE                                     # only if the chosen licence is confirmed
├── requirements.txt                            # environment specification; verify versions
├── RETFound/                                   # compatible upstream RETFound source
├── wbc_project/data/processed/
│   ├── phase2_train/<class>/...
│   ├── phase2_eval/<class>/...
│   └── phase2_test/<class>/...
├── data/external/
│   ├── PBC_dataset_normal_DIB/<class>/...
│   └── Raabin_WBC/
│       ├── Train/...
│       ├── TestA/...
│       └── TestB/{LY,N}/...
├── outputs/
│   ├── final/<model>/seed<seed>/<checkpoint>.pt
│   ├── final_test_v2/<model>/seed<seed>/{true.npy,pred.npy,probabilities.npy,DONE.json}
│   └── asama18_verified_v13/                  # table / figure exports
├── review_results_external_BNE_SNE_v6/       # CNN predictions
├── review_results_ret_found_only_v10/        # corrected RETFound predictions
├── review_results_external_consistency_v13/  # audit / bootstrap
├── review_results_raabin_testb_v1/           # independent TestB analysis
└── review_results_external_per_class_v14/    # external per-class analysis
```

**Important:** External input arrays must be aligned **sample by sample** to the original manifest; never reorder a `pred.npy` array without applying the identical order to `true.npy` and the corresponding paths. The audit notebooks check consistency. Preserve the original dataset split and sample order, and review generated error/issue CSVs before using any table.

## 4. Running the analysis: order and expected artifacts

The exact filenames below reflect the corrected local research workflow. **Before publishing v1.1, ensure every advertised notebook and its imports/supporting source files are committed at the v1.1 tag.** Notebooks working against locally saved predictions are not full from-scratch reproductions of model training.

| Order | Notebook / script | Purpose | Main output |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Original WBCBench training notebooks, including the RETFound seed-42 resume and seeds-1/7 training notebooks | Train/checkpoint models; skip when using provided predictions | `outputs/final/` |
| 2 | `WBCBench_2026_Asama12_v2_Final_Test_Hizli_Progress.ipynb` | Locked WBCBench 13-class evaluation | `outputs/final_test_v2/` |
| 3 | `WBC_External_BNE_SNE_V6_Tam_Analiz.ipynb` | CNN external prediction exports | `review_results_external_BNE_SNE_v6/` |
| 4 | `WBC_RETFound_Only_V10_Dosya_Yollarina_Gore.ipynb` | Corrected RETFound PBC and Raabin Train+TestA prediction exports | `review_results_ret_found_only_v10/` |
| 5 | `WBC_External_V13_Duzeltilmis_Gecerli_Goruntu_Kontrolu.ipynb` | Audit 18 external model–seed–dataset records and recalculate paired intervals | `review_results_external_consistency_v13/` |
| 6 | `WBC_External_PerClass_V14_Reviewer111_CPU_Only.ipynb` | Five-class per-class recall / precision / F1 and corrected confusion matrices | `review_results_external_per_class_v14/` |
| 7 | `Raabin_TestB_Label_Audit_and_2Class_Evaluation_V2_FIXED.ipynb` | Audit TestB labels and, optionally, infer using trained checkpoints | `review_results_raabin_testb_v1/` |
| 8 | `Asama18_Manuscript_Tables_Figures_V2_Verified.ipynb` | Generate tables and main figures from retained results | `outputs/asama18_verified_v13/` |

**Optional WBCBench replay:** `RETFound_WBCBench_V12_Tam_Dogrulama.ipynb` compares saved predictions with a full replay of all three RETFound seeds. The full replay differed in **9 of 98,802** class decisions. This is a near match, **not** strict bitwise/`PASS_FULL` agreement; do not misrepresent it as such.

### Minimum outputs to preserve for reviewer reproducibility

**Summary-level CSVs** (not a substitute for sample-level predictions):

- **V13:** `external_consistency_decision_v13.json`, `external_per_seed_verified_v13.csv`, `external_model_summary_verified_v13.csv`, `external_corrected_seed_average_bootstrap_v13.csv`, `external_audit_issues_v13.csv`.
- **V14:** `external_class_decision_v14.json`, `external_class_per_seed_v14.csv`, `external_class_all_5class_summary_v14.csv`, `external_confusion_5x5_mean_v14.csv`, `external_confusion_5x5_per_seed_v14.csv`, `reviewer_1_11_EO_MO_LY_recall_F1_v14.csv`.
- **TestB:** `testb_preflight_v1.json`, `raabin_train_testa_split_counts_v1.csv`, `testb_two_class_sensitivity_per_seed_v1.csv`, `testb_two_class_sensitivity_summary_v1.csv`, `testb_lymph_neut_recall_v1.csv`, `testb_2x5_confusion_v1.csv`, `testb_inference_issues_v1.csv`.

**Sample-level predictions**, if described in the published paper as available: include the image-order manifest (de-identified relative paths or stable non-sensitive IDs), aligned true labels, model/seed prediction arrays (or a tidy CSV with `sample_id`, `dataset`, `model`, `seed`, `true_class`, `predicted_class`), and the evaluation method. Probability arrays may additionally be shared when licensing/privacy constraints permit. **A class-summary CSV alone is not a sample-level prediction export.** Do not expose local absolute paths, names/patient identifiers, personal data, secret tokens, raw images, or prohibited third-party materials.

Files larger than GitHub's ordinary repository limits can be hosted as **release assets** or via a suitable archival service, with checksums and links in the README. Release assets do not change the Git source snapshot.

## 5. Reference results from corrected local analysis

These values were calculated from the **locally audited** records; they are *not a claim* that a given GitHub release presently contains the corresponding inputs.

### Primary external five-class Macro-F1 (three-seed means)

| Dataset | Model | Baseline | BNE+SNE |
|---|---|---:|---:|
| PBC | ConvNeXt-Tiny | **0.9650** | 0.9628 |
| PBC | ResNet-50 | 0.9255 | 0.9241 |
| PBC | RETFound (corrected) | 0.8734 | 0.8729 |
| Raabin-WBC (Train + TestA) | ConvNeXt-Tiny | **0.7076** | 0.7036 |
| Raabin-WBC (Train + TestA) | ResNet-50 | 0.6209 | 0.6135 |
| Raabin-WBC (Train + TestA) | RETFound (corrected) | 0.4408 | 0.4409 |

### Reviewer 1.11: external class-specific recall

| Dataset | Model | EO recall | MO recall | LY recall |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
| PBC | ConvNeXt-Tiny | 98.37% | 89.58% | 99.20% |
| PBC | ResNet-50 | 98.08% | 68.10% | 99.51% |
| PBC | RETFound | 89.83% | 57.28% | 96.21% |
| Raabin-WBC Train+TestA | ConvNeXt-Tiny | 41.46% | 59.79% | 93.68% |
| Raabin-WBC Train+TestA | ResNet-50 | 17.29% | 47.21% | 84.32% |
| Raabin-WBC Train+TestA | RETFound | 4.28% | 4.82% | 99.64% |

The corrected RETFound confusion matrices show that **70.0% of EO** and **89.5% of MO** Raabin Train+TestA images were predicted as LY, compared with substantially higher EO/MO recall on PBC. This is a descriptive result and does not isolate acquisition, stain, or cohort effects.

### Raabin-WBC TestB: separate sensitivity experiment

| Model | Five-way LY recall | Five-way N recall | Conditional two-class Macro-F1 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| ConvNeXt-Tiny | 90.77% | 88.14% | 0.8794 |
| ResNet-50 | 91.44% | 87.62% | **0.8913** |
| RETFound | **96.62%** | 83.87% | 0.7193 |

The conditional two-class result **cannot** be substituted into or directly compared with the main five-class Macro-F1 ranking. The baseline values above use the five-output rule; a separate BNE+SNE sensitivity is included in the TestB CSVs.

## 6. Environment and reproducibility limits

The local workflow uses Python, Jupyter, NumPy, pandas, scikit-learn, matplotlib, Pillow, and PyTorch/torchvision, together with a compatible RETFound implementation and `timm`. **Training and inference may require different compatible environments.** Do not treat a minimal table-generation `requirements.txt` as proof that RETFound fine-tuning can be reproduced with those dependencies alone. Publish and check the exact package versions, checkpoint format, and compatible upstream RETFound commit when possible.

For inspecting precomputed CSVs and generating figures (no GPU):

```bash
python -m pip install numpy pandas scikit-learn matplotlib pillow jupyter
jupyter notebook
```

This command is **not** a validated environment for all training/inference notebooks. Dataset downloads, fixed checkpoints, class mappings and file manifests remain necessary for independent full reproduction. External V13 auditing validates saved predictions; it does not prove that every checkpoint can be rerun identically in every software environment.

## 7. Publish a correct v1.1 release

**GitHub tag and source snapshot:** A GitHub release is linked to a **Git tag pointing at a specific commit**. GitHub's automatically generated *Source code (zip/tar.gz)* contains the repository files **at that tag**. Uploading `*.ipynb` or `*.csv` as **release assets** only adds downloadable attachments; it does **not** add files to the repository or update its tagged source-code archive.

1. Upload/update `README.md`, `requirements.txt`, `LICENSE` (after confirming your intended licence), notebooks, helper modules and any shareable result CSVs **in the repository**. Commit the changes to your intended branch.
2. Confirm that the repository file list and paths match this README. Run the released notebooks using the documented requirements and data layout, and remove private execution outputs/paths.
3. Go to **Releases → Draft a new release**. Create/select tag **`v1.1`** on the **commit containing the corrected files**, rather than reusing the older v1.0 tag.
4. Optionally add bigger prediction archives or supplementary outputs as downloadable **release assets**, with a manifest and checksums. A published *immutable release* may not allow later changes to its assets or tag; assemble the complete draft first.
5. Publish the release. Verify **Source code (zip)** includes the new `README.md`, notebooks, `requirements.txt` and licence, and that any declared release assets are downloadable.
6. **Only after publication and verification**, update manuscript *Code Availability*, *Data Availability* and the reviewer response to point to `https://github.com/sara-altun/WBC-Transfer-Evaluation/releases/tag/v1.1`. Do not cite a future/empty release as already public.

GitHub references: [About releases](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/releasing-projects-on-github/about-releases), [Managing releases](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/releasing-projects-on-github/managing-releases-in-a-repository).

